Am I doing something wrong here? claude and codex couldn't figure it out either. lol

```
@OptIn(ExperimentalCalfUiApi::class)
@Composable
fun BlurryTabBarRepro() {
    var selectedIndex by remember { mutableIntStateOf(0) }

    val icons = listOf(
        Icons.Default.Home,
        Icons.Default.Settings,
        Icons.Default.Person,
    )
    val labels = listOf("Home", "Settings", "Account")

    AdaptiveNavigationBar(
        iosItems = icons.mapIndexed { index, icon ->
            UIKitUITabBarItem(
                title = labels[index],
                image = UIKitImage.Vector(icon),
                selectedImage = UIKitImage.Vector(icon),
            )
        },
        iosSelectedIndex = selectedIndex,
        iosOnItemSelected = { selectedIndex = it },
        iosConfiguration = UIKitTabBarConfiguration(
            isTranslucent = true,
        ),
    ) {
        icons.forEachIndexed { index, icon ->
            NavigationBarItem(
                selected = selectedIndex == index,
                onClick = { selectedIndex = index },
                icon = { Icon(icon, contentDescription = null) },
                label = { Text(labels[index]) },
            )
        }
    }
}
```

my icons are standard Android vector drawable XML files, not SVGs.

according to claude

"CALF’s blurry result happens with Compose ImageVector input, including vectors loaded from Android vector drawable XML.
In my case, the icons are monochrome stroked vector drawables at 24dp.
The issue is specific to iOS [UIKitImage.Vector(...)](app://-/index.html#); the same assets look sharp in regular Compose rendering."

### Description

1. The `BottomNavigationBar` disappears only after a delay, when navigating to a screen without a bottom bar.
2. When navigating back from a screen without the bottom navigation bar, -> it becomes visible immediately, even if the gesture is not completed yet.

> Only on iOS. Issue is not present when using material scaffold and navigation bar.
>
> Usecase example: logout functionality from within a menu tab.

```kotlin
# Navigation
NavDisplay(
    backStack = backstack,
    entryProvider = entryProvider {
         entry<Route.Tabs> {
             TabsScreen(onButtonClick = { backstack.add(Route.Example) })
         }
         entry<Route.Example> {
              ExampleScreen()
          }
    }
)

# Screen with bottom navigation
@Composable
private fun TabsScreen() {
    AdaptiveScaffold(
        bottomBar = {
            AdaptiveNavigationBar(
                iosSelectedIndex = 0,
                iosItems = listOf(
                    UIKitUITabBarItem(title = "Tab 1"),
                    UIKitUITabBarItem(title = "Tab 2"),
                ),
                iosOnItemSelected = {},
            ) {
                NavigationBar { ... }
            }
        },
    ) {
        ...
    }
}

# Screen without navigation bar
@Composable
private fun ExampleScreen() {
    AdaptiveScaffold {
        Box(contentAlignment = Alignment.Center, modifier = Modifier.fillMaxSize()) {
            Text("Example Screen")
        }
    }
}
```

### Environment

> Compose Multiplatform project with Android/iOS targets.

```kotlin
# libs.versions.toml
agp = "9.0.1"
composeMultiplatform = "1.11.1"
